---
import { withBase } from "../lib/paths";
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../assets/maverick.png';
---
<Layout title="About" section="About">
  <header class="page-heading about-intro">
    <Image class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Maverick" width={320} format="webp" />
    <div><p class="eyebrow">A little about me</p><h1>Hi! I’m Maverick.</h1><p class="about-welcome">Welcome to my space for all things data, analytics, and AI/ML engineering.</p></div>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>I’m curious about how data becomes something useful, from the pipelines and models behind it to the analytics and AI/ML applications people use.</p>
    <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
    <p>I’ll share practical notes, walkthroughs, and ideas on working with data, building analytics, and exploring AI/ML engineering. Tools like dbt and Microsoft Fabric will show up along the way, too.</p>
    <p>Some posts will work through a specific problem. Others will be questions I’m still figuring out.</p>
    <h2>Why I write</h2>
    <p>Writing helps me make sense of what I’m learning. This blog is a place to think things through, share useful discoveries, and keep coming back with new questions.</p>
    <hr />
    <p>Have a look through <a href={withBase("/writing/")}>my posts</a>, pick a topic in the sidebar, or <a href={withBase("/rss.xml")}>follow along via RSS</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 160px; align-items: center; gap: 32px; }
  .portrait { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1; display: block; width: 160px; height: auto; border-radius: 6px; }
  .about-intro > div { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; }
  .about-welcome { color: var(--muted); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .about-intro { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    .portrait { grid-column: 1; grid-row: 1; width: 128px; }
    .about-intro > div { grid-row: 2; }
  }
</style>
